Make the local-multiplayer transport count the frames it carries.

WHY. Two consoles now bring the cartridge's own wireless stack all the way up -
one reaches WH_SYSSTATE_DATASHARING, the other WH_SYSSTATE_SCANNING - and they
never find each other. Three explanations were available:
the transport carries nothing, the two radios sit on different channels, or a
parent already in DATASHARING does not accept new children.

Nothing could tell them apart, because the transport is SILENT. Both instances
log "[local_mp] enabled" at startup and then never say anything again, so a
transport carrying zero frames looks exactly like one carrying thousands. That
is the same un-measurable claim this project keeps having to withdraw, and it
is cheap to fix: count them and say so.

Geometric backoff on the logging - 1, 4, 16, 64 ... - so a live transport
announces itself within the first frames and then goes quiet, rather than
printing at 60 Hz for a whole run. The receive line names the SENDING instance,
because "instance 1 received a frame from instance 0" is the fact in question
and "a frame arrived" is not.

--- a/runner/src/wifi_net.cpp
+++ b/runner/src/wifi_net.cpp
@@ -866,6 +866,16 @@
                          reinterpret_cast<sockaddr*>(&target),
                          sizeof(target)) != SOCKET_ERROR) {
                 sent = len;
+                ++tx_frames_;
+                // Geometric, so a live transport says so early and
+                // then goes quiet instead of logging at 60 Hz.
+                if (tx_frames_ >= tx_logged_ * 4u + 1u) {
+                    tx_logged_ = tx_frames_;
+                    melonDS::Platform::Log(melonDS::Platform::Info,
+                        "[local_mp] instance %u SENT %llu frame(s)\n",
+                        static_cast<unsigned>(instance_),
+                        static_cast<unsigned long long>(tx_frames_));
+                }
             } else if (send_error_log_counter_ < 8u) {
                 ++send_error_log_counter_;
                 melonDS::Platform::Log(melonDS::Platform::Warn,
@@ -917,6 +927,16 @@
             frame.payload.assign(datagram + kHeaderBytes,
                                  datagram + kHeaderBytes + len);
 
+            ++rx_frames_;
+            if (rx_frames_ >= rx_logged_ * 4u + 1u) {
+                rx_logged_ = rx_frames_;
+                melonDS::Platform::Log(melonDS::Platform::Info,
+                    "[local_mp] instance %u RECEIVED %llu frame(s), from %u\n",
+                    static_cast<unsigned>(instance_),
+                    static_cast<unsigned long long>(rx_frames_),
+                    static_cast<unsigned>(frame.sender));
+            }
+
             const uint32_t low_type = frame.type & 0xFFFFu;
             if (low_type == 2u)
                 reply_queue_.TryPush(std::move(frame));
@@ -941,6 +961,14 @@
     LocalMpFrameQueue reply_queue_{kQueueCapacity};
     int last_host_id_ = -1;
     uint32_t send_error_log_counter_ = 0;
+    // DOES ANYTHING ACTUALLY CROSS BETWEEN THE INSTANCES? Two consoles
+    // can both report enabled at startup and still never exchange a
+    // frame, and nothing counted them - so a silent transport was
+    // indistinguishable from a working one.
+    uint64_t tx_frames_ = 0;
+    uint64_t rx_frames_ = 0;
+    uint64_t tx_logged_ = 0;
+    uint64_t rx_logged_ = 0;
 #ifdef _WIN32
     SOCKET socket_ = INVALID_SOCKET;
 #endif
